[
  {
    "id": "g-ser",
    "title": "ser",
    "summary": "to be: who or what someone is",
    "intro": [
      "Ser means \"to be\" for what someone or something is: name, nationality, job, character, and also the time.",
      "It's irregular, so the forms have to be learnt by heart."
    ],
    "table": [
      { "person": "eu", "form": "sou" },
      { "person": "tu", "form": "és" },
      { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "é" },
      { "person": "nós", "form": "somos" },
      { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "são" }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Eu sou inglês.", "en": "I'm English. (a woman says inglesa)" },
      { "pt": "A Rita é professora.", "en": "Rita is a teacher." },
      { "pt": "Nós somos amigos.", "en": "We're friends." },
      { "pt": "São oito horas.", "en": "It's eight o'clock." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "No \"a\" before jobs: Sou estudante = I'm a student.",
      "Você exists, but in Portugal it can sound distant or even rude. Use tu with friends; with strangers use o senhor / a senhora, or just the verb: É de Lisboa?",
      "Vós (an old form of \"you all\") is only heard in some northern regions. This app uses vocês."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "person": "eu", "answer": "sou" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "tu", "answer": "és" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "ela", "answer": "é" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "nós", "answer": "somos" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "eles", "answer": "são" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "vocês", "answer": "são" },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "Eu ", "after": " de Londres.", "answer": "sou", "en": "I'm from London." },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "A Rita ", "after": " professora.", "answer": "é", "en": "Rita is a teacher." },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "Tu ", "after": " muito simpático.", "answer": "és", "en": "You're very nice." },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "Nós ", "after": " portugueses.", "answer": "somos", "en": "We're Portuguese." },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "O João e a Ana ", "after": " irmãos.", "answer": "são", "en": "João and Ana are brother and sister." },
      { "type": "sentence", "before": "", "after": " oito horas.", "answer": "São", "en": "It's eight o'clock." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-estar",
    "title": "estar",
    "summary": "to be: how or where someone is now",
    "intro": [
      "Estar also means \"to be\", but for how or where something is right now: feelings, health, location, weather and other states that change."
    ],
    "table": [
      { "person": "eu", "form": "estou" },
      { "person": "tu", "form": "estás" },
      { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "está" },
      { "person": "nós", "form": "estamos" },
      { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "estão" }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Estou cansado.", "en": "I'm tired. (a woman says cansada)" },
      { "pt": "Onde estás?", "en": "Where are you?" },
