      { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "têm" }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Tenho vinte anos.", "en": "I'm twenty. (literally: I have twenty years)" },
      { "pt": "Tens irmãos?", "en": "Do you have brothers or sisters?" },
      { "pt": "Temos fome.", "en": "We're hungry." },
      { "pt": "Ela tem frio.", "en": "She's cold." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "têm (they have) has a hat on the e; tem (he or she has) doesn't. They sound almost the same.",
      "Tenho de + verb = I have to: Tenho de trabalhar. In Portugal you'll mostly hear tenho de; Brazilians usually say tenho que."
    ],
